hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16322","He said: Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zam'ah, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning women, and he admonished concerning them, and said: For what does one of you beat his wife, and perhaps he may lie with her at the end of the day or the end of the night."
"16323","He said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zam'ah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the most wretched of them rose, there rose for it a strong, mighty, invincible man among his clan, like Abu Zam'ah. Then he admonished them about laughing at flatulence, and said: At what does one of you laugh at what he does? He said: Then he said: At what does one of you flog his wife with the flogging of a slave, then perhaps he may lie with her at the end of his day."
"16324","He said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zam'ah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached, and mentioned the she-camel and mentioned the one who hamstrung it, and said: When the most wretched of them rose, there rose for it a strong, mighty, invincible man among his clan, like Abu Zam'ah. Then he mentioned women and admonished them concerning them, and said: For what does one of you flog his wife with the flogging of a slave, and perhaps he may lie with her at the end of his day? Then he admonished them about their laughing at flatulence, and said: For what does one of you laugh at what he does?"
"16325","Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zam'ah: He admonished them concerning women, and said: For what does one of you beat his wife with the beating of a slave, then he lies with her at the end of the night."
